    {
      "id": "tutorial-core-concepts-what-is-a-node-graph-s1",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "What it is",
      "position": {
        "x": -270,
        "y": -200
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "What it is",
        "body": "**A Graph Holds Things And Relationships**\n\nA node graph is not just a pile of boxes. It is a system for saying:\n\n- these are the things\n- these are the relationships\n- these relationships are explicit, not implied\n\n**Nodes Hold Meaning**\n\nA node is a discrete unit. It can represent an idea, decision, example, step, person, file, view, or contract. Because the unit is discrete, you can move it, inspect it, reference it, and change it without rewriting everything around it.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-core-concepts-what-is-a-node-graph"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
