    {
      "id": "tutorial-core-concepts-what-is-a-node-graph-s3",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Why it lasts",
      "position": {
        "x": 2130,
        "y": -200
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "Why it lasts",
        "body": "**Structure Survives Growth**\n\nAs work becomes more complex, flat notes become harder to keep coherent. A graph can grow by adding nodes and relationships without collapsing the whole thing into one long, fragile block of text.\n\n**One Graph Can Hold Many Depths**\n\nThe same graph can support overview, reference, workflow, examples, and detail. You do not have to move the work into a second medium just because it became more serious.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-core-concepts-what-is-a-node-graph"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
