    {
      "id": "tutorial-core-concepts-what-is-a-node-graph-s5",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Check yourself",
      "position": {
        "x": 930,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "Check yourself",
        "body": "**When Is A Graph Better?**\n\nTry to answer this in one sentence:\n\nA node graph is more powerful than a paragraph when ____________________.\n\nIf your answer does not mention relationships, navigation, or structural growth, return to the concept cards above.\n\n**Checkpoint**\n\nYou are done with this lesson when you can explain that a node graph is powerful not because it draws boxes, but because it preserves units of meaning and the relationships between them in a form that can be navigated and extended.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-core-concepts-what-is-a-node-graph"
